      "label": "The older woman is mapped as someone who goes on ancestry.com instead of match.com",
      "description": "The text overlay 'goes on ancestry.com instead of match.com' creates an analogical mapping where the visual entity 'older_woman' is implicitly identified as the person engaging in the activity described in the text. The meme humorously suggests that the woman, through her focused expression and use of the laptop, is participating in genealogical research (ancestry.com) rather than online dating (match.com). This mapping is established by the juxtaposition of the text with the visual of the woman using the laptop, implying she is the subject of the action described in the text.",
